  "changed_since_previous": "No substantial changes to the approach or mechanism; the logic in `CWallet::ResubmitWalletTransactions` and configuration loading remains the same.",
  "card": "Suppresses unconfirmed wallet transaction resubmission to the mempool when running with -privatebroadcast. Currently, when the network evicts a transaction, a wallet periodically re-adds it to the local mempool and serves it to peers upon request, identifying the node as the transaction's originator or recipient over clearnet. Skipping resubmission on startup, import, and timer intervals prevents deanonymizing users who opted into private broadcast. Initial transaction broadcasts remain unaffected.",
